    {
      "id": "ElZHb42A5wcuKAWaNgb-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 271.5104064941406,
      "y": 177.17446899414062,
      "width": 1177.8124694824219,
      "height": 1600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 746943908,
      "version": 2129,
      "versionNonce": 113867556,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792042442411,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional requirements\n    1. Continous ingest of structured or unstructured logs from the client.\n    2. Search anf filter the logs based on time , service, severity, full-text within 15 days of hot window and can have 1\nyear of cold storage.\n    3. Define custom alert rules and trigger notitfication\n    4. Configure retention policies as per the user service or lo levels.\n    \nNon - Fucntional Requirements :\n    1. High Throughput\n    2. Low latency search - sub ms as only 15  days of window for search\n    3. Scalability and fault tolerence\n\nBack of the envelope :\n    Ingestion Throughput - 100k logs/sec * 1 KB = 100 MB/sec\n    Daily Raw Ingestion - 100 MB/sec * 86,400s ~ 8.6 TB/day\n    Hot Storage (15 Days) - (8.6 TB + 20% index) * 2 replicas * 15d ~ 300 TB (SSD/HDD)\n    Cold Storage (2 Years) - (8.6 TB * 20% compressed size) * 730d ~ 1.24 PB (S3)\n    \nEntities and Data Models :\n    1. log : log_id(PK), client_id, timestamp, status,service_name, level, trace_id, message- Cold Storage so it will be a S3\nbucket\n    2. Hot log DB : ELS  : timestamp, service_name, level, trace_id, message\n    3. Config DB : Postgre : services table : id, name, hot_retention_days, cold_retention_days\n                                   alert_rules : id, service_id, log_level, thrshold_count, webhook_url \n\nAPI Designing :\n    1. Ingestion : POST : v1/logs/batch \n                    { \"service_name\" :...\n                       \"env\": ...\n                        \"logs\" :[{},{},{}]\n                        }\n    2. Search : POST : v1/logs/search\n                     { \"service_name\" :...\n                       \"env\": ...\n                        \"levels\" : [ERROR, FATAL]\n                        \"query\" :[...]\n                        }\n    3. Rehydration : POST : v1/logs/rehydrate\n                        { \"service_name\" :...\n                       \"env\": ...\n                        \"start_time\" : ...\n                        \"end_time\" : ....\n                        }\n    4. Config : POST : v1/config/alerts\n                { \"service_name\": \"payment-service\",\n                  \"rule_name\": \"High Gateway Timeout Failure\",\n                  \"log_level\": \"ERROR\",\n                  \"pattern_match\": \"GATEWAY_TIMEOUT\",\n                  \"threshold_count\": 50,\n                  \"time_window_seconds\": 300,\n                  \"notification_channel\": {\n                    \"type\": \"SLACK\",\n                    \"target_url\": \"https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00/B00/XXXXXX\"\n                  }\n    \n    5. Retention : PUT /v1/config/retention\n                {\n                    \"service_name\": .....,\n                      \"hot_retention_days\": ....,\n                      \"log_level\": \"ERROR\",\n                      \"cold_retention_days\": ...,\n                      }\n    \nHigh Level Design :",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional requirements\n    1. Continous ingest of structured or unstructured logs from the client.\n    2. Search anf filter the logs based on time , service, severity, full-text within 15 days of hot window and can have 1 year of cold storage.\n    3. Define custom alert rules and trigger notitfication\n    4. Configure retention policies as per the user service or lo levels.\n    \nNon - Fucntional Requirements :\n    1. High Throughput\n    2. Low latency search - sub ms as only 15  days of window for search\n    3. Scalability and fault tolerence\n\nBack of the envelope :\n    Ingestion Throughput - 100k logs/sec * 1 KB = 100 MB/sec\n    Daily Raw Ingestion - 100 MB/sec * 86,400s ~ 8.6 TB/day\n    Hot Storage (15 Days) - (8.6 TB + 20% index) * 2 replicas * 15d ~ 300 TB (SSD/HDD)\n    Cold Storage (2 Years) - (8.6 TB * 20% compressed size) * 730d ~ 1.24 PB (S3)\n    \nEntities and Data Models :\n    1. log : log_id(PK), client_id, timestamp, status,service_name, level, trace_id, message- Cold Storage so it will be a S3 bucket\n    2. Hot log DB : ELS  : timestamp, service_name, level, trace_id, message\n    3. Config DB : Postgre : services table : id, name, hot_retention_days, cold_retention_days\n                                   alert_rules : id, service_id, log_level, thrshold_count, webhook_url \n\nAPI Designing :\n    1. Ingestion : POST : v1/logs/batch \n                    { \"service_name\" :...\n                       \"env\": ...\n                        \"logs\" :[{},{},{}]\n                        }\n    2. Search : POST : v1/logs/search\n                     { \"service_name\" :...\n                       \"env\": ...\n                        \"levels\" : [ERROR, FATAL]\n                        \"query\" :[...]\n                        }\n    3. Rehydration : POST : v1/logs/rehydrate\n                        { \"service_name\" :...\n                       \"env\": ...\n                        \"start_time\" : ...\n                        \"end_time\" : ....\n                        }\n    4. Config : POST : v1/config/alerts\n                { \"service_name\": \"payment-service\",\n                  \"rule_name\": \"High Gateway Timeout Failure\",\n                  \"log_level\": \"ERROR\",\n                  \"pattern_match\": \"GATEWAY_TIMEOUT\",\n                  \"threshold_count\": 50,\n                  \"time_window_seconds\": 300,\n                  \"notification_channel\": {\n                    \"type\": \"SLACK\",\n                    \"target_url\": \"https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00/B00/XXXXXX\"\n                  }\n    \n    5. Retention : PUT /v1/config/retention\n                {\n                    \"service_name\": .....,\n                      \"hot_retention_days\": ....,\n                      \"log_level\": \"ERROR\",\n                      \"cold_retention_days\": ...,\n                      }\n    \nHigh Level Design :",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
